course: dictionary
lesson: 6709
title: Of: the tiny word with many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Of» is one of the smallest words in English, but it does lots of jobs. It links a part to the whole it belongs to: «Some children are adopted» means some of all children, and «a piece of cake» means one piece from the cake.
explain: «Of» can show what something holds or is made of: «a cup of tea», «a box of crayons», or a table made of wood. It can also show who or what something is about: «the name of the dog» or «a story of a giant».
explain: In maths, «of» often means times. «Half of 12» means 12 ÷ 2, which is 6, and «3 groups of 4» means 3 times 4, which is 12. Look at the clues: packs, rows and groups usually mean multiply.
explain: In speech, «of» is squeezed: «kinda» is kind of, «lotta» is lot of, and «cuppa» is cup of tea. In writing, do not write «should of» or «could of». Write «should've» or «should have» instead.
fact: Of links a part to a whole, shows what something holds or is made of, and shows who or what something is about.
fact: In «some hot springs smell of it too», of means they give off the same smell.
fact: «Half of 12» means 12 ÷ 2, which is 6.
fact: «3 out of 10» means 3 parts of a whole that has 10 parts.
fact: In exam writing, «of» is piled up: «the product of 3 and 4» means 12, and «the quotient of 12 and 4» means 3.
exercise: «A piece of cake» is one part of a whole cake. What job does of do here? | *It links a part to the whole it belongs to | It shows a date | It is a short form of «off» | It means times
exercise: What does of show in «a box of crayons»? | It means times | It shows a date | *It shows what the box holds | It shows who the box belongs to
exercise: What is «half of 12»? | 2 | 24 | *6 | 12
test: In «the name of the dog», what does of show? | It means times | It shows a time of day | It shows the dog is made of wood | *It shows who or what the name is about
test: Which is correct in writing? | *I should've come | I should outta come | I should off come | I should of come
exam: In the exam voice, what is «the product of 3 and 4»? | 1 | 34 | *12 | 7
